    {
      "name": "Decade-Long Southeast Asia / India Espionage (FireEye APT30 Report)",
      "year_published": null,
      "description": "FireEye documented over a decade of APT30 operations targeting government and commercial entities across Southeast Asia and India. The group focused on political, economic, and military intelligence, with special emphasis on ASEAN-related targets, South China Sea territorial disputes, India-China relations, and journalists covering Chinese government issues. Social engineering lures were crafted around ASEAN summits (notably January and April 2013) and regional security topics. The group used ASEAN-themed infrastructure and customized malware, deployed BACKSPACE and NETEAGLE backdoors via spear-phishing, and employed SHIPSHAPE/SPACESHIP/FLASHFLOOD to cross air-gapped networks. FireEye identified activity at an Indian aerospace/defense company and an Indian telecom firm.\n",
      "target_sectors": [
