          "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20220512021812/https://www2.fireeye.com/rs/fireye/images/rpt-apt30.pdf",
          "title": "APT30 and the Mechanics of a Long-Running Cyber Espionage Operation",
          "publisher": "FireEye"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Malaysia / Thailand Targeting (PT Security)",
      "year_published": null,
      "description": "PT Security detected renewed APT30 activity starting in August 2019 with a NETEAGLE dropper disguised as a Malaysian government meeting agenda (AGENDA.scr, created by user \"Norehan Binti Nordin\"). The dropper deployed an updated NETEAGLE variant (internal string changed to \"JokerPlay\") and BACKSPACE backdoors with new string encryption algorithms. Samples were uploaded from Malaysia to VirusTotal. Additional infrastructure analysis revealed two new backdoor families (RHttpCtrl, RCtrl) sharing C2 infrastructure (gordeneyes.com, kabadefender.com) with the classic tools, confirming operational continuity.\n",
      "target_sectors": [
        "government"
      ],
      "target_regions": [
        "Malaysia"
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://global.ptsecurity.com/en/research/pt-esc-threat-intelligence/eagle-eye-is-back-apt30/",
          "title": "The eagle eye is back: old and new backdoors from APT30",
          "publisher": "PT Security"
        }
      ]
    }
